What this licence covers, and what it does not

The text above covers this repository's own files: the adapter, the core's
own display, sound and platform layers and the test runners under waterbox/,
the build files, and the documents.

The patches under patches/ are changes to Fuse and are under Fuse's terms,
the GNU General Public License version 2 or later.

It does not cover what the repository builds from. The emulator is Fuse, the
Free Unix Spectrum Emulator, by Philip Kendall and others
(https://fuse-emulator.sourceforge.net/), with its library libspectrum, both
under the GNU General Public License version 2 or later, at the commits
pinned in extern/fuse and extern/libspectrum. zlib (extern/zlib) is under
the zlib licence. Fuse contains Blip_Buffer and the SNES NTSC filter by Shay
Green, under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 or later.

The built package, fuse.chimeraCore, is therefore under the GNU General
Public License version 2 or later. waterbox/package-licenses.json lists every
component with its licence and where its source is, and the built package
carries their licence texts.

No ROM of any computer is in this repository or in the package. Fuse's own
source tree has a roms/ directory with the Spectrum's ROMs, which Amstrad
allows to be distributed with emulators, and others; this core does not
package them. A user supplies the ROMs of the machine they choose. The tests
read ROMs from a folder outside the repository, and on a machine with none
they use only the two ROMs of the ZX Spectrum SE (OpenSE BASIC, GNU GPL
version 2 or later), which they read from the pinned Fuse submodule.

No game is in this repository or in the package.
